.TH PMX "1" "October 2026" "PMXViewer v0.2.1+GLFW3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pmx \- MikuMikuDance PMX/PMD model / VMD motion viewer (MikuMikuPenguin)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pmx
[\fB\-s\fR \fImusic\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIcamera.vmd\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fIlight.vmd\fR] [\fB\-\-loop\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-gui\fR] {\fImodel.pmx\fR|\fImodel.pmd\fR} [\fImotion.vmd\fR] [\fB\-\-pos\fR \fIX,Y,Z\fR] [\fImodel2\fR [\fImotion2.vmd\fR] ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pmx
(PMXViewer) is a demonstration program for the MikuMikuPenguin library
(libmmp).  It loads a PMX 2.0 or PMD model and plays a VMD motion on it, with
Bullet physics for hair, skirts and other rigid bodies.
Camera and light motion are played, and the model visibility and IK on/off
keys of the motion file are honoured.  Like MMD, the model casts a ground
shadow and a self shadow (shadow map) following the light.
.PP
An OpenGL 3.2 core profile capable driver is required.
.PP
Several models can be played together: each VMD file belongs to the model
given before it (a model without a VMD stays in its rest pose).  All models
share the time line, the camera and the light; each has its own physics
(models do not collide with each other).  Motions made for several dancers
usually contain each dancer's position already.
.PP
Files can also be opened while the viewer runs: from \fBFile\fR on the
playback bar (add a model, a motion for a model, camera or light motion,
music), from the settings panel (motion / remove for each model), or by
dropping them onto the window (PMX/PMD = add a model, VMD = motion for the
first model without one, or camera/light motion when the VMD has no bone or
morph keys, other files = music).  Without file arguments the viewer starts
empty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-pos\fR \fIX,Y,Z\fR
Position of the preceding model, in MMD coordinates (also adjustable in the
settings panel).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR \fIfile\fR
Play a music file along with the VMD motion.
Only formats supported by SDL2_mixer are accepted.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fIfile\fR
Camera motion (a VMD file with camera frames).  Without this option the
camera frames contained in the motion file, if any, are used.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR \fIfile\fR
Light motion (a VMD file with light frames).  Without this option the light
frames of the \fB\-c\fR file are used, then those of the motion file.
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\fR
Restart from the beginning when the end of the motion (its last key) is
reached.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gui\fR
Start with the on-screen controls hidden (\fBTab\fR shows them).
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
display help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
output version information and exit
.SH CONTROLS
A playback bar (play/pause, seek, frame step, timeline, loop) is shown at the
bottom of the window, and its \fBSettings\fR button opens a panel with the
display options and a list of these shortcuts.  The labels are Japanese when
the locale is Japanese and a Japanese font is installed.
.TP
.B Tab
show / hide the on-screen controls
.TP
.B Left mouse drag
rotate the camera
.TP
.B Mouse wheel
zoom in / out
.TP
.B Up / Down
move the model up / down
.TP
.B Q (hold)
pause the physics simulation
.TP
.B A (hold)
hide the model
.TP
.B S, D, F, G (hold)
Bullet debug drawing (wireframe, AABB, constraints, constraint limits)
.TP
.B C
toggle the VMD camera motion (moving the camera with the mouse switches to the free camera)
.TP
.B Space
pause / resume (the music too)
.TP
.B Left / Right
seek 1 second back / forward (with Shift: 10 seconds); the physics restarts
from the new pose
.TP
.B , / .
one frame back / forward (pauses playback)
.TP
.B Home / End
go to the beginning / end of the motion
.TP
.B O
toggle looping
.TP
.B Z
toggle the ground shadow
.TP
.B X
toggle the self shadow (also switched by the self shadow keys of the VMD)
.TP
.B L
toggle the VMD light motion (off: MMD default light)
.TP
.B R
reset the camera (front view framing the whole model)
.TP
.B Esc
quit
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/mikumikupenguin/shaders/
GLSL shaders (a \fIshaders/\fR directory in the current directory takes
precedence).
.TP
.I /usr/share/mikumikupenguin/textures/
shared toon textures toon01.bmp \- toon10.bmp.
.TP
.I /usr/share/mikumikupenguin/doc/README_JP.html
Japanese documentation.
.TP
.I log.txt
created in the current directory.
